# Backend — FastAPI + SQLAlchemy Rules

## Architecture
- Entry point: `backend/app/main.py` (lifespan, middleware, routers)
- All routes registered in `backend/app/api/v1/api.py`
- New routers → add to api.py at bottom with comment
- Services in `backend/app/services/` — pure business logic, no HTTP imports
- Repositories in `backend/app/repositories/` — DB queries only

## Dependency Injection Pattern
```python
# Always use these in order:
db: Session = Depends(get_db)
user = Depends(get_current_user)           # any authenticated user
user = Depends(require_roles("owner"))     # owner + superadmin
user = Depends(require_superadmin)         # superadmin only
farm_ids = Depends(get_scoped_farm_ids)    # multi-tenant scoping
```

## Cache Pattern
```python
from app.core.cache import cached, cache_delete

@router.get("/items")
@cached("items", ttl=300)  # 5 minutes
def list_items(...):
    ...

@router.post("/items")
def create_item(...):
    cache_delete("items:*")  # invalidate after write
    ...
```

## Error Handling
- Use `HTTPException(status_code, detail)` in endpoints
- Use `logger.warning()` in services for non-critical failures
- Never let unhandled exceptions reach the client

## DB Migrations (SQLite-safe)
```python
from sqlalchemy import inspect, text
insp = inspect(engine)
cols = [c['name'] for c in insp.get_columns('table_name')]
with engine.connect() as conn:
    if 'new_column' not in cols:
        conn.execute(text("ALTER TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN new_column VARCHAR(100)"))
        conn.commit()
```

## Scheduler Jobs (APScheduler)
- Add new jobs in `backend/app/core/scheduler.py`
- Jobs registered in `start_scheduler()` function
- Always use `replace_existing=True` to avoid duplicates

## Push Notifications
```python
from app.services.push_service import send_to_user, broadcast_push, notify_alert
# FCM_SERVER_KEY must be set in .env
send_to_user(db, user_id, "Title", "Body", {"key": "value"})
```
